---
title: Terms and conditions
description: The terms for using nullish, the service provided by Fluster GmbH.
---

These terms govern the use of nullish, provided by Fluster GmbH, Zürich ("we"). By creating an account or using nullish, you accept them.

## Scope

These terms apply to the Cloud plan and to anyone using nullish. For a dedicated instance or an on-premises installation, the agreement we sign with you takes precedence. These terms apply wherever it says nothing.

The source code of nullish is open source under the MIT license. These terms cover the service we run, not the code.

## Account

You need an account to use nullish. Give accurate information and keep your sign-in details to yourself. You're responsible for what happens with your account.

Each organization has its own subscription and its own admins. Admins decide who has access and with which role.

## Service

nullish lets you issue invoices, import and reconcile bank statements, keep your accounting and compute VAT, with an AI assistant, a REST API and an MCP server. The [documentation](/en/getting-started/) describes what it does.

We keep improving nullish, so features may change. We do our best to keep it running, but can't guarantee it's always available. Maintenance, updates and outages are announced on [nullishstatus.com](https://nullishstatus.com) whenever possible.

## Trial

A new organization may start with a free trial. If it ends without a plan, the organization is locked: its data can't be accessed until it has a plan again.

## Prices and payment

The prices are listed on the [pricing page](/en/pricing/), in Swiss francs, excluding VAT.

A subscription is paid in advance for the chosen period, monthly or yearly, and renews automatically. Payments are processed by Stripe.

If a payment fails, a banner shows the date the organization will be locked. Update the payment method before then and everything goes on as usual.

## Price changes

We announce price changes by email at least 30 days in advance. They apply from the next billing period. If you don't agree, you can cancel before then.

## Cancellation

You can cancel at any time under **Subscription**. The subscription keeps running until the end of the period already paid. Periods already started aren't refunded.

We can terminate an account, after a warning where reasonable, if it's used unlawfully or in breach of these terms.

## Your data

Your data stays yours. We process it only to provide nullish, and acting on your behalf. The [privacy policy](/en/privacy/) explains how.

When an admin deletes an organization, it becomes read-only, at the latest at the end of the period already paid. It's deleted for good, with all its data, 30 days later.

nullish doesn't replace your duty to keep your business records. Under Swiss law, you must keep them for 10 years. Make sure you keep a copy, for example through the REST API.

## AI assistant

The assistant's answers are generated by an AI model and can be wrong. Check them before relying on them. They don't replace the advice of a fiduciary or a tax expert.

We don't use your data to train AI models.

## Your responsibilities

You're responsible for the content of your accounting, your invoices and your VAT returns.

Don't use nullish for unlawful purposes, don't try to access other people's data and don't overload the service, including through the API and the MCP server. Keep your API keys secret.

## Liability

As far as the law allows, we exclude any liability, in particular for negligence, indirect or consequential damage, lost profit and data loss. This also applies to the subcontractors and people we work with.

In any case, our liability is limited to the fees you paid in the 12 months before the damage occurred.

We're not liable for services provided by third parties, such as banks or payment providers.

## Changes to these terms

We may change these terms. We announce changes by email at least 30 days before they take effect. If you don't agree, you can cancel before then.

## Severability

If a provision of these terms is invalid, the others remain valid. The invalid provision is replaced by one that comes as close as possible to its purpose.

## Governing law and jurisdiction

These terms are governed by Swiss law. The courts of Zürich have exclusive jurisdiction.

## Contact

Questions about these terms? Write to [hi@nullish.ch](mailto:hi@nullish.ch).
